## The two adaptations

Every adopted body is byte-for-byte upstream except these two, and each keeps its
upstream bytes everywhere else:

1. `inclusive-interaction/skills/touch-target-design/SKILL.md`, in "Minimum
   Sizes", says the touch floor is `44x44 CSS pixels (WCAG 2.2 Level AA)`. That
   pairs a size with the wrong level: WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum) is
   Level AA at 24x24 CSS px, and SC 2.5.5 Target Size (Enhanced) is Level AAA at
   44x44. The adopted copy states 24x24 as the AA floor with its success
   criterion and keeps 44x44 as the AAA floor and the common platform guideline.
   That is the floor tezgah's own `bin/tezgah-design` enforces - `TAP_TARGET =
   24`, citing SC 2.5.8 - so the vendored copy and the checker now agree. The
   file's other 44x44 mentions (its touch checklist, the Material
   recommendation) state no level and are kept as upstream wrote them.
2. `cognitive-accessibility/skills/adaptive-personalisation/SKILL.md` carries
   `name: contextual-help-design`, which does not match its directory: it is the
   duplicate of the sibling `contextual-help-design` skill, body included. A host
   that loads a skill from its directory skips a name that disagrees with it, so
   the adopted copy's `name` is `adaptive-personalisation`. The body, its
   "Contextual Help Design" heading included, is upstream's.

## What is not, and why

- The account's other collections: `ux-pgm-skills` (30) and
  `design-leadership-skills` (32) are one generator's ~1 KB checklists that cite
  no external standard anywhere, and `ai-design-skills` (44) is about designing
  AI products rather than about a tezgah turn. The other three plugins of
  `inclusive-design-skills` - `accessible-content`, `accessibility-decisions`,
  `inclusive-personas`, 26 skills - are left out too: `design-contract`,
  `feature-audit` and the WCAG floor cover that ground, and every one of them is
  one URL away.
- `designer-skills`' design-research plugin beyond the two vendored skills, 12
  more (`affinity-diagram`, `journey-map`, `survey-design`, ...): the funnel and
  triangulation discipline is what tezgah has no counterpart for; the synthesis
  workshops are not.
- Each adopted skill's own `EVALS.md`, upstream's for the two design-research
  skills: this library ships one `EVALS.md` for the tree instead, in the same
  shape.
- The plugin packaging surface of both repositories - `.claude-plugin/*.json`,
  `commands/`, the READMEs, the marketplace manifest - the same rule
  `skills/pm-frameworks` states.
- `habitat` is read for the shape of a checker, never vendored: its component and
  tokens JSON schemas are the shape `bin/tezgah-design` reads a design contract
  as. No habitat prose or code is copied.

## Re-vendoring

Copy the two pinned checkouts' files over the tree, re-apply the two adaptations
above, replace every sha256 in the table, and update the revisions in this file -
all in one commit. `tests/test_skills.py` fails on a body that no longer matches
its hash, on a listed file that is missing, and on a directory beside them the
table does not list, so a re-vendor that moves only the files is caught.
